      "originalText": "day18: Debouncing, throttling, and code-splitting \nToday i leart debouncing throttling, and code-splitting working. \nfor implementation debouncing I get product data from fakeStore\napi using axios and disply on title of product on ui. then \ni created input for serach product title and disply searched product\ntitle on ui. so for that i get input value and store in serach state\nthen i match with product state title using map and show on ui, \nbut i seen every search word state update and every time filtered\ndata function call, for preventing I used useEffect but in dependcy\ni need to write run function on every serchaData state, so also\nthat function run. so for that setTimeout() to fun function after\n700 sec after that i use useeffect cleanup function to clear\ntimeout so after every 700 sec function run and when user type\nword in between 700 sec so it's show only run function once\nbecasue of it's clear past interval when new come:\ncode of debouncing for searching title from api.\n // debouncing\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!searchData) return;\n    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {\n      filteredData();\n    }, 700);\n    return () => clearTimeout(timeout);\n  }, [searchData]);\n\n\nthroutling: throutling is use in lazy loading when we \nscroll our page so lot of event trigger we for prenventing\nthat there is use throutling concept. this is code of \nthat:\n useEffect(() => {\n    const handleScroll = () => {\n      if (throttle) return;\n      throttle = true;\n      console.log(\"scrolling...\");\n      setScrollY(window.scrollY);\n\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        throttle = false;\n      }, 5000);\n    };\n\ncode splitting: \ncode splitting when our web site open so all compenent\nopen in one go, so it's take time to open web site, \nso for that i used code splitting concept here on about\nand contact page, when i click of about or contact then\nit's load that component so only necessory components\nload first time so our web site not take time for open.\nthis is code splitting concept code:\nconst AboutPage = lazy(() => import(\"../pages/AboutPage\"));\nconst ContactPage = lazy(() => import(\"../pages/ContactPage\"));\n\nalso i leant loader concept on any route component when data\ncomming form api it's take time so when first come data and then\ncomponent render we used loader concept, loader first check \ndata come then render the comonent. on loader take callback \ninside call we give function of api call, and we need to write also \nhydrateFallbackElement. like below code.\nhydrateFallbackElement: <h1>Api loding...</h1>, \nalso i learnt suspense element for when data then show component\n element: (\n            <Suspense fallback={<h1>About loding...</h1>} >\n              <AboutPage />\n            </Suspense>\n          ),\n\n\n\n",
